WEBVTT


00:00:29.644 --> 00:00:32.704
<i>Hold on 'cause I'm letting go</i>


00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.316
<i>I'm gonna lasso your heart like a rodeo</i>


00:00:36.484 --> 00:00:40.147
<i>I'm gonna give you some
Till you want some more</i>


00:00:40.321 --> 00:00:44.052
<i>'Cause all I see is an open door</i>


00:00:44.225 --> 00:00:48.025
<i>And I see where it's leading me
All of this energy</i>


00:00:48.195 --> 00:00:51.790
<i>Been bottled up way too long
It's powerful, powerful</i>


00:00:51.966 --> 00:00:55.527
<i>You see what I'm getting at
I'm ready for all of that</i>


00:00:55.703 --> 00:00:59.230
<i>If I'm not a star, you're blind</i>


00:00:59.407 --> 00:01:02.774
<i>I've got rings on my fingers
And glitter in my hair</i>


00:01:02.944 --> 00:01:06.209
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:10.077
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:10.251 --> 00:01:14.278
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:14.455 --> 00:01:18.050
<i>I've got high heel stilettos
And I'm kicking in doors</i>


00:01:18.225 --> 00:01:21.353
<i>And kissing your ass
Ain't what my lipstick's for</i>


00:01:21.529 --> 00:01:25.295
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:25.466 --> 00:01:28.458
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:28.636 --> 00:01:32.128
Where's breakfast?
I want waffles, spaghetti!


00:01:32.306 --> 00:01:35.571
Spaghetti waffles! Whoo. Whoo!


00:01:35.743 --> 00:01:37.768
Victor. Victor.
Please wait in the house, please.


00:01:39.213 --> 00:01:42.046
My body is entering hunger shock.


00:01:43.417 --> 00:01:47.114
Oh, bad news.
The cat pooped in the den.


00:01:47.288 --> 00:01:50.587
Worse news, I used your blanket
to clean it up.


00:01:50.758 --> 00:01:52.692
- We don't have a cat.
- No kidding.


00:02:27.795 --> 00:02:31.356
Oh. L... Sorry.
I didn't think you'd be awake.


00:02:31.532 --> 00:02:32.692
You have an appointment...


00:02:32.867 --> 00:02:35.461
...with Guy Morgan,
I didn't think you'd wanna be late.


00:02:35.636 --> 00:02:38.571
Oh, look at you thinking. Cute.


00:02:38.739 --> 00:02:40.798
But I always have time for my portrait.


00:02:40.975 --> 00:02:42.499
Look alive. Paint.


00:02:42.943 --> 00:02:44.774
I'm feeling spiritually blocked.


00:02:44.945 --> 00:02:46.776
Draw me a sesame seed bath.


00:02:47.214 --> 00:02:48.340
Bath. Now.


00:02:49.316 --> 00:02:51.181
Now, make momma look more beautiful
and thinner.


00:02:52.553 --> 00:02:53.781
And make that water more quiet.


00:02:57.358 --> 00:02:59.451
- Bev, you awake?
- Of course I'm awake.


00:02:59.627 --> 00:03:02.221
If I waited for you, I'd never be on time.


00:03:02.396 --> 00:03:04.830
Lucky you never wait for me then.


00:03:18.312 --> 00:03:19.745
Victor, no.


00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.354
Uh, don't you want a glass?


00:03:28.522 --> 00:03:34.518
Hmm. Earthy. A tad fishy.
Lovely gravel finish.


00:03:34.995 --> 00:03:37.520
Did you let Victor put worms
in the blender again?


00:03:38.232 --> 00:03:39.927
Yes. I mean, no.


00:03:41.435 --> 00:03:43.027
I mean, it just happened.


00:03:43.571 --> 00:03:44.936
You know nothing can kill me.


00:03:46.107 --> 00:03:47.734
Nothing.


00:03:52.379 --> 00:03:55.246
Step on it, Katie.
I cannot be late for this meeting.


00:03:55.416 --> 00:03:56.781
Just run them over if you have to.


00:03:59.587 --> 00:04:02.613
Hello? No, the kids don't need a library.


00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:06.021
I am the dean, and the dean gets
what she wants, and I wanna remodel.


00:04:06.193 --> 00:04:09.651
You're just boring. I'm being honest.
I don't know what else to tell you.


00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:12.924
And I wanted my office done
for my meeting with Guy Morgan...


00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:14.761
...the music mogul, but no.


00:04:14.935 --> 00:04:17.130
And using Bollywood
as a theme for the dance?


00:04:17.304 --> 00:04:20.762
That's totally un-American.
I don't care if it was my idea.


00:04:22.443 --> 00:04:24.707
Hello.
Oh. Oh.


00:04:24.879 --> 00:04:27.575
I'm Dean Van Ravensway,
and you must be...


00:04:27.748 --> 00:04:30.842
- Guy Morgan.
- Ah, yes. Guy Morgan, a pleasure.


00:04:31.018 --> 00:04:32.508
You look like a man who knows things.


00:04:32.686 --> 00:04:35.246
Aha, even some things I shouldn't know.


00:04:35.422 --> 00:04:37.219
- And I'm Luke.
Great.


00:04:50.771 --> 00:04:54.730
<i>So tell me, Guy, is it true?
Are you the new judge on Idol?</i>


00:04:54.909 --> 00:04:58.276
Well, let's just say
that Randy may be in the doghouse.


00:04:58.445 --> 00:05:00.310
- Now, let's talk about my son.
- Of course.


00:05:00.481 --> 00:05:02.915
- Have you reviewed your schedule, Luke?
- Yes, I have.


00:05:03.083 --> 00:05:06.610
In fact, um, I'd like to add a music class.
Um, the music theory...


00:05:06.787 --> 00:05:10.348
Wellesley has a great business program.
That's why we're here.


00:05:10.858 --> 00:05:15.761
There are two types of people
in the music biz: Artists and businessmen.


00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:17.761
- Luke is a businessman.
- Of course.


00:05:18.265 --> 00:05:22.258
Katie, get in here. Look alive.
Make yourself useful.


00:05:25.739 --> 00:05:28.071
Luke is gonna need a tour of the campus.


00:05:28.542 --> 00:05:33.605
So text Bev and ask her
to escort Mr. Morgan around campus.


00:05:33.914 --> 00:05:37.042
Now, Luke, if you are half as talented
a producer as your father...


00:05:37.218 --> 00:05:40.278
The verdict's still out.
He hasn't earned it.


00:05:41.956 --> 00:05:44.220
Heard the story of how I started
in the music business?


00:05:44.391 --> 00:05:47.827
- Yes, everybody's heard it, Dad.
- Then everybody should know how it goes.


00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:52.324
There I was,
working for The Rolling Stones...


00:05:52.499 --> 00:05:54.330
...when Mick himself...
- Dad.


00:05:55.603 --> 00:05:58.800
Fine. As I said,
the verdict is still out on my son.


00:05:58.973 --> 00:06:02.739
He just produced an album
with the Fruity Dangers?


00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:04.571
Do you mean Danger Fruit?


00:06:05.746 --> 00:06:07.509
That record was amazing.


00:06:07.681 --> 00:06:10.650
I forgot what they were called because
they made me absolutely no money.


00:06:12.152 --> 00:06:14.620
Thank you. Rare I meet anyone
who's heard their album.


00:06:14.788 --> 00:06:17.689
What, are you kidding?
They're a cult phenomenon.


00:06:17.858 --> 00:06:19.519
I'm sorry. Why are you talking?


00:06:21.061 --> 00:06:26.624
What I need is for Luke to learn
to spot a commercially viable star.


00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:28.961
Image drives the bottom line, right?


00:06:29.136 --> 00:06:32.503
I feel you. Would we have Bieber Fever
if he were an ugly troll?


00:06:32.673 --> 00:06:34.834
Actually, he is a tad hobbit-like, isn't he?


00:06:35.009 --> 00:06:37.375
I'd like Luke
to produce your Semester Showcase...


00:06:37.544 --> 00:06:41.446
...to see if he can identify sellable talent.
- I produce the Semester Showcase.


00:06:42.583 --> 00:06:44.676
I will double your Showcase budget.


00:06:45.185 --> 00:06:47.551
I will invite every talent scout I know.


00:06:48.122 --> 00:06:50.249
This could be the beginning
of a relationship...


00:06:50.424 --> 00:06:52.392
...between Wellesley
and Kensington Records.


00:06:52.559 --> 00:06:54.550
Looks like we have a new producer.


00:06:54.728 --> 00:06:57.697
Oh, and this is my daughter, Bev.


00:06:58.132 --> 00:07:00.896
Bev, this is the platinum-selling,
Grammy-winning...


00:07:01.068 --> 00:07:03.969
...and very handsome producer,
Guy Morgan.


00:07:04.138 --> 00:07:05.969
Could you give his son, Luke, a tour?


00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:09.007
Sure. Would you like
to see the Wellesley perks?


00:07:09.176 --> 00:07:11.804
Um, yes, brilliant. Sure.


00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:14.270
- Katie.
I love your accent.


00:07:14.448 --> 00:07:16.040
Katie.
Wanna come over tonight?


00:07:16.216 --> 00:07:18.582
What are you still doing here? Go.


00:07:18.752 --> 00:07:22.153
Guy and I have things we need to discuss.
Out. Now.


00:07:22.756 --> 00:07:28.160
So, Guy, you've gotta tell me,
what was that like working under Mick?


00:07:37.037 --> 00:07:38.732
Watch out.


00:07:39.206 --> 00:07:41.231
- Dangerous balls.
- Ha, ha. Thanks.


00:07:42.242 --> 00:07:45.837
- So you womanned up and did it?
Hey!


00:07:46.013 --> 00:07:47.810
- Oh, I did it.
Hey!


00:07:47.981 --> 00:07:50.347
- What happened?
Can we have our ball?


00:07:50.517 --> 00:07:51.882
I didn't give my CD to Luke.


00:07:52.052 --> 00:07:55.044
I snuck it in his dad's bag.


00:07:55.222 --> 00:07:59.181
But Guy Morgan has your demo.
That's huge. What you need is a champion.


00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:01.089
No, what I need is to graduate.


00:08:01.929 --> 00:08:03.829
You giving our ball back or what?


00:08:03.997 --> 00:08:07.626
Oh, do you want this?


00:08:12.439 --> 00:08:15.704
She shoots, she scores.
Unlike you, soccer boy.


00:08:18.045 --> 00:08:21.776
Oh, so spill it. Is Luke Morgan
as hot as everyone Tweets he is?


00:08:21.949 --> 00:08:23.314
Hotter.


00:08:23.484 --> 00:08:25.111
You should ask him to the dance.


00:08:25.285 --> 00:08:27.515
Because I'm so forward with guys.


00:08:27.688 --> 00:08:30.248
First time for everything, right?


00:08:37.398 --> 00:08:39.093
- Hi, Luke.
- Hello.


00:08:39.266 --> 00:08:40.494
You have to hear my demo.


00:08:40.968 --> 00:08:44.028
It's a retro-funk-jazz explosion.


00:08:44.204 --> 00:08:46.399
Back off. I was here first.


00:08:46.573 --> 00:08:50.031
Hold on, hold up. Please hold on.
My boy does not want your demos yet.


00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:52.474
Walk away. Move along. Bye.


00:08:52.646 --> 00:08:56.013
It was nice chatting
or whatever that was.


00:08:56.283 --> 00:08:58.615
- Yes, hi, I'm, uh...
- Luke Morgan, right?


00:08:58.786 --> 00:09:00.310
Who is producing the Showcase.


00:09:00.487 --> 00:09:03.388
I don't think I'm gonna do the Showcase,
so I need to keep a low profile...


00:09:03.557 --> 00:09:06.993
Yeah, yeah. Listen close now.
There's two kinds of people in this school.


00:09:07.161 --> 00:09:10.688
There are the wannabes
and there's gonnabes.


00:09:10.864 --> 00:09:16.029
You and I, we're gonnabes. What do we do?
We stay away from the wannabes, all right?


00:09:16.203 --> 00:09:19.764
And girls named Yolanda. There are three
of them and they are certifiably...


00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:22.033
Crazy? You attract
crazy women? Shocking.


00:09:22.209 --> 00:09:25.110
It may seem like I don't have game,
but ladies love a listener.


00:09:25.279 --> 00:09:27.406
Plus, I'm telling you,
let me help you find acts.


00:09:27.581 --> 00:09:30.607
- Ah, so you're a talent scout?
- Well, bottom line, I'm a DJ.


00:09:30.784 --> 00:09:32.979
- Oh, you're a DJ as well?
- Check this.


00:09:41.528 --> 00:09:42.790
Whoa.


00:09:42.963 --> 00:09:46.057
Okay, yes. You could be very useful.
It was nice meeting you.


00:09:46.233 --> 00:09:48.895
You got a girl for the dance?
Because I can hook you up.


00:09:49.069 --> 00:09:50.229
Uh, no. Thanks.


00:09:50.404 --> 00:09:53.805
Uh, but what do you know
about Bev Van Ravensway?


00:09:53.974 --> 00:09:55.635
- Supposed to see her tonight.
- Bev?


00:09:55.809 --> 00:09:56.833
- Yeah.
- She's hot...


00:09:57.010 --> 00:09:59.478
...but the girl
is mad, mad drama, okay?


00:09:59.646 --> 00:10:02.046
I am talking to you
and you don't even know my name.


00:10:02.216 --> 00:10:04.116
- I'm Mickey O'Malley.
- Mickey O'Malley.


00:10:04.284 --> 00:10:05.911
A rarity in the Irish community.


00:10:06.487 --> 00:10:08.580
Om.


00:10:09.389 --> 00:10:12.017
RAVl: Om.
- Om.


00:10:12.192 --> 00:10:14.285
- Om.
- Om!


00:10:14.461 --> 00:10:16.986
This is not a contest, Ms. Gail.


00:10:17.364 --> 00:10:18.991
Just concentrate on your breathing.


00:10:20.501 --> 00:10:21.661
My butt is numb.


00:10:22.002 --> 00:10:25.199
If your butt is suffering,
then you are suffering.


00:10:25.372 --> 00:10:28.830
In fact, your entire life is suffering. Why?


00:10:29.009 --> 00:10:32.103
Because you crave
that which is meaningless.


00:10:32.279 --> 00:10:34.270
Are you calling me shallow?


00:10:35.349 --> 00:10:41.185
No, I'm saying to stop your craving
and release your butt.


00:10:41.355 --> 00:10:44.916
Just release it. Release it, yeah.
Release that butt.


00:10:45.792 --> 00:10:48.852
<i>Release that butt
Oh, yeah, release that butt</i>


00:10:49.029 --> 00:10:51.623
<i>Oh, yeah, release that butt</i>


00:10:51.798 --> 00:10:53.095
Mrs. Van Ravensway?


00:10:53.267 --> 00:10:55.792
What part
of "if you interrupt my meditation...


00:10:55.969 --> 00:10:59.166
...I will jerk your tail in a knot"
do you not understand?


00:10:59.339 --> 00:11:01.773
You told me
to tell you when dinner was ready.


00:11:01.942 --> 00:11:05.343
Oh, thank God.
I'm craving some bourbon.


00:11:09.116 --> 00:11:10.583
Victor.


00:11:10.751 --> 00:11:15.984
- Oh. Um, dinner's ready.
- Tell me something I don't know.


00:11:39.646 --> 00:11:44.083
Do you have any idea how stressful it is
to run this academy?


00:11:44.418 --> 00:11:46.909
Yes, I spent the money at the spa.


00:11:47.955 --> 00:11:50.617
<i>Five thousand dollars a night
is not very expensive...</i>


00:11:50.791 --> 00:11:55.353
<i>... when you think about the alternative,
which is me having a nervous breakdown.</i>


00:11:58.665 --> 00:11:59.689
<i>Ow.</i>


00:11:59.866 --> 00:12:02.300
<i>What are you doing?
I'm on the phone.</i>


00:12:02.469 --> 00:12:04.061
<i>- I'm cleansing.
Heh, heh.</i>


00:12:04.271 --> 00:12:06.501
Mac and cheese.


00:12:07.407 --> 00:12:10.535
<i>I don't need your spiritual counseling.</i>


00:12:11.078 --> 00:12:12.636
<i>I'm thinking of firing you.</i>


00:12:18.151 --> 00:12:21.518
Pace yourself, Ms. Gail,
or you will not be one with everything.


00:12:21.688 --> 00:12:25.021
Honey, that's what I got you for.
Now, make me one with everything.


00:12:26.426 --> 00:12:29.623
This Showcase is giving me the vapors.


00:12:29.796 --> 00:12:31.889
How did this become my life?


00:12:32.065 --> 00:12:35.057
Did I ever tell you all about the time
I nearly got my big break?


00:12:35.235 --> 00:12:36.725
Yes.
- Good.


00:12:36.903 --> 00:12:38.336
Then you all know how it goes.


00:12:38.772 --> 00:12:40.967
<i>I ain't gonna leap, I'm gonna jump</i>


00:12:41.141 --> 00:12:43.473
<i>Find my way right out of this dump</i>


00:12:46.313 --> 00:12:49.180
- I had talent, and they made me...
A laughingstock.


00:12:50.951 --> 00:12:52.248
Now look at me.


00:12:52.419 --> 00:12:54.910
I got two ungrateful kids...


00:12:55.088 --> 00:12:58.080
...a dwarfish, hairy, elfin servant...


00:12:58.258 --> 00:13:00.249
...and a random
tablecloth-wearing Asian...


00:13:00.427 --> 00:13:02.657
- Indian.
- Who makes no sense at all, ever.


00:13:02.829 --> 00:13:04.592
Why don't you have another drink, Mom.


00:13:06.133 --> 00:13:08.328
Katie, napkin me.


00:13:08.502 --> 00:13:10.993
I have got to impress Guy Morgan...


00:13:11.405 --> 00:13:14.636
...so I can stop pretending to care
about this insufferable school...


00:13:14.808 --> 00:13:18.574
...and we can all move to Hollywood where
no one pretends to care about anything.


00:13:18.745 --> 00:13:22.374
Mom, I think that you're forgetting
about the most important thing. Me.


00:13:23.316 --> 00:13:25.716
Guy will give me a deal
as soon as he hears me sing.


00:13:25.886 --> 00:13:28.480
- I doubt that.
- No, I've been practicing really hard.


00:13:28.655 --> 00:13:31.522
My voice teacher says
I've transcended to a whole new level.


00:13:31.692 --> 00:13:32.716
Yeah, I doubt it.


00:13:32.893 --> 00:13:35.453
When my first single drops,
I'll buy you that mansion...


00:13:35.629 --> 00:13:37.563
...in the Hollywood Hills...


00:13:37.731 --> 00:13:40.757
...and you can finally afford
to have your legs lengthened.


00:13:40.934 --> 00:13:42.959
- Oh, ba...
- Ms. Gail.


00:13:43.136 --> 00:13:45.104
- Miss Bev has clarity.
Katie.


00:13:45.272 --> 00:13:46.296
- You see...
- Look.


00:13:46.473 --> 00:13:50.341
- The lowly peasant tills the soil
for 40 years without any rain.


00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:53.911
But the unemployed salesman
who has recently discovered hydroponics...


00:13:54.081 --> 00:13:57.175
...all of a sudden gets disgusted by the...
- And see? No sense.


00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:59.648
- That didn't make any sense.
- Let me finish. You...


00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:01.754
Oh, I doubt it. You have me pray all day.


00:14:01.922 --> 00:14:04.152
- I don't feel nothing.
- You don't have a soul.


00:14:04.324 --> 00:14:07.521
No, you don't have soul.
- I have a many souls. I'll give you one.


00:14:07.694 --> 00:14:11.960
- Where's your third eye? Turn that thing on.
- I have a fourth eye too. You wanna see it?


00:14:12.132 --> 00:14:14.100
- What?
- Shh.


00:14:14.601 --> 00:14:18.128
I wanna be 6'4". Wow me, Bev.


00:14:20.674 --> 00:14:26.112
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:26.279 --> 00:14:28.839
Just stop. Stop the wowing, okay?


00:14:29.015 --> 00:14:31.108
What's wrong?
- Somehow you've gotten worse.


00:14:31.284 --> 00:14:33.013
I don't know how that was possible...


00:14:33.186 --> 00:14:35.814
...but there isn't enough Auto-Tune
that's gonna fix you.


00:14:35.989 --> 00:14:39.322
- Well, Katie's bad playing threw me off.
- I don't think it was that.


00:14:39.493 --> 00:14:41.120
Again.


00:14:41.294 --> 00:14:42.852
Really? Okay.


00:14:43.029 --> 00:14:48.661
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:48.835 --> 00:14:49.961
Ouch.


00:14:50.137 --> 00:14:53.197
I could belch the song better.


00:14:54.808 --> 00:14:56.969
Have you been drinking
the floor wax again?


00:14:57.144 --> 00:14:58.611
Anything to forget I live here.


00:14:58.779 --> 00:15:01.680
Ugh. My head is buzzing
like a skeeter on a septic tank.


00:15:01.848 --> 00:15:05.750
- Ravi, meditate me.
Good luck, buddy.


00:15:06.119 --> 00:15:09.782
Well, it doesn't matter,
because I have my own plan.


00:15:13.994 --> 00:15:16.360
Does it make me a bad person
that I kind of enjoyed that?


00:15:16.530 --> 00:15:18.259
No.


00:15:18.431 --> 00:15:20.729
Hmm. Nice work.


00:15:32.913 --> 00:15:36.212
- Guess who's on his way over.
- Not now, Victor, I'm busy.


00:15:36.383 --> 00:15:38.851
Guess or prepare to get creamed.


00:15:49.329 --> 00:15:52.423
Victor! Victor! Victor, stop!


00:15:57.304 --> 00:15:59.033
<i>I've got rings on my fingers</i>


00:15:59.206 --> 00:16:00.298
<i>And glitter in my hair</i>


00:16:00.473 --> 00:16:04.569
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:16:04.744 --> 00:16:06.075
<i>I'm gonna run...</i>


00:16:06.246 --> 00:16:09.010
- Ha-ha-ha.
- Victor, what are you doing?


00:16:09.449 --> 00:16:10.746
Victor!


00:16:10.917 --> 00:16:14.148
Victor, where did you put my clothes?


00:16:14.321 --> 00:16:16.482
- Surprise!
- What? No.


00:16:19.993 --> 00:16:21.620
I'm gonna kill you. Victor!


00:16:31.538 --> 00:16:32.698
Oh, hi, Katie.


00:16:32.873 --> 00:16:34.272
You are evil. Let me in.


00:16:34.441 --> 00:16:37.877
I control every lock on this property.


00:16:38.044 --> 00:16:39.705
Crap.


00:16:43.116 --> 00:16:44.811
This is insane.


00:16:44.985 --> 00:16:49.046
Yeah, try the shed, it's unlocked, idiot.


00:16:58.832 --> 00:17:00.925
You gotta be kidding me.


00:17:02.669 --> 00:17:04.296
Crap.


00:17:07.607 --> 00:17:11.202
How did such an untalented daughter
spring from my loins?


00:17:11.378 --> 00:17:15.178
Focus, Ms. Gail. We are making
an offering to your personal deity.


00:17:15.348 --> 00:17:17.475
Tell him to give me fame and fortune.


00:17:17.651 --> 00:17:19.346
Not exactly how it works.


00:17:19.519 --> 00:17:22.079
<i>Now, breathe through your Mula Bandha.</i>


00:17:22.255 --> 00:17:25.315
Oh, honey, if I could do that,
I'd get a million hits on YouTube.


00:17:25.492 --> 00:17:27.722
How much longer is this gonna take?
Ugh.


00:17:27.894 --> 00:17:30.021
The prayer or the fame and fortune?


00:17:32.365 --> 00:17:33.832
Ha, ha. See you later.


00:17:40.006 --> 00:17:41.871
Victor.


00:17:45.712 --> 00:17:47.145
Katie?


00:17:48.348 --> 00:17:50.578
- Luke.
- Katie.


00:17:50.784 --> 00:17:54.049
- Are you wearing a doormat?
- Yes.


00:17:54.220 --> 00:17:56.984
- Welcome.
- Why, thank you.


00:17:58.024 --> 00:17:59.855
The truth. Um...


00:18:01.161 --> 00:18:04.494
My stepbrother locked me
outside of the house.


00:18:04.664 --> 00:18:05.995
Naked.


00:18:07.033 --> 00:18:09.331
Oh, sorry. You should...
You should take my jacket.


00:18:09.502 --> 00:18:11.026
Oh.
- Oh, no, no.


00:18:13.473 --> 00:18:14.565
There.


00:18:14.741 --> 00:18:17.938
- Thanks. Now the pants.
- Hmm?


00:18:22.549 --> 00:18:24.176
I'm kidding.


00:18:24.718 --> 00:18:26.549
- You got me.
- Ha, ha.


00:18:26.886 --> 00:18:27.910
No, no.


00:18:28.088 --> 00:18:31.489
One more parent-teacher conference,
I swear I'm gonna lose it.


00:18:31.658 --> 00:18:33.853
Look at me. I'm an educator.


00:18:34.461 --> 00:18:39.125
I have no real skills. And I will die
before I go back to my daddy's farm.


00:18:39.632 --> 00:18:43.432
You tell my personal deity
to help me achieve Guy Morgan. Do it.


00:18:43.603 --> 00:18:46.197
I'll put another banana on the altar.


00:18:50.076 --> 00:18:51.737
What is that?


00:18:52.312 --> 00:18:54.576
Do you hear angels singing?


00:18:54.748 --> 00:18:56.716
Perhaps the gods
have answered your prayer.


00:18:57.917 --> 00:18:59.646
Hey. What...?


00:19:12.499 --> 00:19:14.990
<i>- This is Gail Van Ravensway.
Hello.</i>


00:19:15.168 --> 00:19:16.795
Guy Morgan here. How are you?


00:19:16.970 --> 00:19:19.097
Oh, well, hello, Guy.


00:19:19.272 --> 00:19:21.536
What a surprise
to see you calling this number.


00:19:21.708 --> 00:19:22.732
Do you hear this?


00:19:22.909 --> 00:19:24.570
<i>I can justify</i>


00:19:24.744 --> 00:19:26.439
That's the demo your girl, Katie...


00:19:26.613 --> 00:19:28.945
<i>... slipped into my briefcase.</i>


00:19:29.115 --> 00:19:31.310
And it sounds like money, dear.


00:19:31.484 --> 00:19:33.349
She gave you a CD?


00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:36.887
Oh, well. Well, ain't that the berries.


00:19:38.124 --> 00:19:41.992
Ravi, what frigging god did you pray to?


00:19:43.229 --> 00:19:47.325
Guy, yeah, it seems someone's
not being entirely honest here.


00:19:49.302 --> 00:19:51.497
Katie, somebody get that door!


00:19:52.639 --> 00:19:54.197
So...


00:19:55.075 --> 00:19:57.202
...that meeting today...


00:19:57.377 --> 00:20:00.175
...it was obvious
that your dad doesn't get you.


00:20:00.513 --> 00:20:02.572
He's an idiot for not liking your music.


00:20:02.749 --> 00:20:05.183
Well, it's... It's complicated.


00:20:05.452 --> 00:20:06.646
I'm gonna just, uh...


00:20:08.121 --> 00:20:10.021
Is it as complicated as me...


00:20:10.190 --> 00:20:13.318
...getting stuck outside
in only a welcome mat?


00:20:13.593 --> 00:20:17.324
That's not complicated.
That is a gift from God.


00:20:22.235 --> 00:20:25.033
Luke. Katie. What are you doing?


00:20:25.205 --> 00:20:28.265
Well, it seems your brother
is Satan's very own personal Mini-Me.


00:20:28.441 --> 00:20:30.705
Oh, I know, tell me about it. Come on in.


00:20:34.681 --> 00:20:36.342
Oh, my God, did you work out today?


00:20:38.017 --> 00:20:39.314
- Sit down.
- Ooh, look at this.


00:20:39.486 --> 00:20:42.580
- Ha, ha. Some lemonade.
- Why, thank you.


00:20:42.755 --> 00:20:45.223
You know, my stepsister,
she has body issues...


00:20:45.391 --> 00:20:47.552
...so I don't like
to discourage her nudity.


00:20:47.727 --> 00:20:48.921
That's interesting.


00:20:49.095 --> 00:20:51.859
- She's absolutely lovely...
- Would you like an appetizer?


00:20:52.031 --> 00:20:53.259
<i>Oh, fromage.</i>


00:20:53.433 --> 00:20:55.060
I only have cheese.


00:20:58.238 --> 00:21:00.206
I just got off the phone
with Guy Morgan.


00:21:00.373 --> 00:21:02.273
Your phone.


00:21:05.311 --> 00:21:08.178
He just loved that little demo
you left him.


00:21:08.348 --> 00:21:09.906
I have underestimated you.


00:21:10.483 --> 00:21:12.314
It'd make me proud
if I cared about you.


00:21:12.485 --> 00:21:15.579
- I didn't lie about anything.
- Oh, but, chicken, you did.


00:21:15.755 --> 00:21:18.383
At least that's what Guy thinks,
now that I've clarified.


00:21:18.558 --> 00:21:22.756
I told him it was Bev's demo
and that you stole it from her.


00:21:22.929 --> 00:21:26.194
- But you can't do that. That's my song.
- It's Bev's song.


00:21:26.366 --> 00:21:29.802
And Guy can't wait to see her perform it
at the Showcase.


00:21:29.969 --> 00:21:33.097
If you try to contact him, I'll deny
everything and lock you in the basement.


00:21:33.273 --> 00:21:38.404
- She can't sing to save her life.
- No, but you can, can't you?


00:21:39.679 --> 00:21:41.840
Now, let's hear this amazing voice.


00:21:47.253 --> 00:21:51.883
<i>Like a malignant tumor
She's got no sense of humor</i>


00:21:52.058 --> 00:21:56.154
<i>Just like a swollen blister
It's best to just resist her</i>


00:21:56.329 --> 00:22:00.095
<i>She's not exactly a witch
She's just a terrible bi...</i>


00:22:00.567 --> 00:22:02.228
Well, your lyrics stink.


00:22:02.402 --> 00:22:04.563
But Guy's right, you've got chops.


00:22:07.807 --> 00:22:10.503
Do you know what other instruments
I'm good at?


00:22:11.077 --> 00:22:14.535
I have a feeling I could get in trouble
with a question like that.


00:22:14.981 --> 00:22:16.949
I like trouble.


00:22:18.484 --> 00:22:19.610
Hey, kids.


00:22:20.920 --> 00:22:24.356
- Good evening, Miss Van Ravensway.
- Sorry, I need you to go. Now.


00:22:24.524 --> 00:22:27.288
Family emergency. I need Bev
to help me pass a kidney stone.


00:22:27.460 --> 00:22:31.294
- So she had a lovely evening. Ta-ta.
- Are you trying to ruin my life?


00:22:31.598 --> 00:22:36.831
I have figured out a way for you
to wow Guy Morgan in the Showcase.


00:22:37.036 --> 00:22:39.504
- So you do think I've improved?
- Oh, no, honey.


00:22:39.772 --> 00:22:42.332
But my month of spiritual devotion
has taught me...


00:22:42.508 --> 00:22:44.476
...that God works in annoying ways.


00:22:44.644 --> 00:22:47.704
How am I to wow Guy Morgan
if I supposedly can't sing?


00:22:47.880 --> 00:22:50.940
You can't, but Katie can.


00:22:51.117 --> 00:22:53.813
- What?
- I know. Like I said, annoying.


00:22:53.987 --> 00:22:57.286
We'll record her voice
and you will lip synch.


00:22:57.457 --> 00:22:59.288
What if I don't want to?


00:23:00.393 --> 00:23:04.124
Don't you get snarky with me,
you ungrateful toad.


00:23:04.297 --> 00:23:06.356
- I saved your life.
- You didn't do anything.


00:23:06.532 --> 00:23:08.796
- My dad married you.
- Yeah, and then he died.


00:23:08.968 --> 00:23:12.529
I tried to put you in foster care,
but they was all fulled up on ugly.


00:23:12.705 --> 00:23:14.195
- Funny.
- I thought it was...


00:23:14.374 --> 00:23:15.841
...because you don't wanna look bad.


00:23:17.443 --> 00:23:19.570
Katie, if you don't sing...


00:23:19.746 --> 00:23:22.874
...I'm gonna find a way for that savings
your dad left to disappear.


00:23:23.283 --> 00:23:27.481
That means, you forget college,
moving out, you're stuck here with me.


00:23:27.654 --> 00:23:31.488
But, pumpkin, we're gonna have
so much fun growing old together.


00:23:31.658 --> 00:23:34.559
Why don't you just have her perform
if you like her so much?


00:23:34.727 --> 00:23:36.991
Because, honey, look at you.


00:23:37.163 --> 00:23:39.290
You are a star.


00:23:39.465 --> 00:23:43.663
That is what Guy Morgan needs.
You, the star.


00:23:43.836 --> 00:23:45.394
I'm a star.


00:23:45.571 --> 00:23:49.735
- A bright, gassy star.
- Yes, you are.


00:23:49.909 --> 00:23:52.309
And Guy Morgan is gonna
give you a swimming pool...


00:23:52.478 --> 00:23:54.446
...shaped just like Colin Farrell.


00:23:54.614 --> 00:23:56.172
Every part of him.


00:23:56.349 --> 00:23:59.876
Or, Bev, you could just see every part
of Colin Farrell on the Internet.


00:24:00.053 --> 00:24:02.817
And just leave me out of this.


00:24:04.090 --> 00:24:06.650
- Okay, so how do we do this?
- First rule of Lie Club...


00:24:06.826 --> 00:24:08.726
...is don't talk about Lie Club.


00:24:09.329 --> 00:24:11.229
Which includes you, Katie.


00:24:11.397 --> 00:24:14.093
As far as everyone knows,
you can't sing.


00:24:14.267 --> 00:24:16.326
And no more talking to Luke or Guy.


00:24:16.502 --> 00:24:17.867
Are we clear?


00:24:18.304 --> 00:24:19.498
Crystal.


00:24:21.441 --> 00:24:24.433
Yeah, Dad, we're about to meet
some fresh talent right now.


00:24:24.610 --> 00:24:28.603
Remember when you signed Jay-Z?
No, you passed on him, my bad.


00:24:28.781 --> 00:24:31.249
Um, this is like that,
except it's gonna be brilliant.


00:24:31.417 --> 00:24:32.748
Yeah. Okay.


00:24:32.919 --> 00:24:35.046
- Yeah, okay. Bye.
- Dude, what'd he say?


00:24:35.221 --> 00:24:36.745
These guys you told me about are good?


00:24:36.923 --> 00:24:40.290
Yes. The Oral Majority has potential.
They'll be here any second.


00:24:40.460 --> 00:24:43.156
Talking about potential,
how was your little date with Bev?


00:24:43.329 --> 00:24:45.593
- Her mom kicked me out.
- I told you. Bev is drama.


00:24:45.765 --> 00:24:47.323
Technically, it was Gail's drama.


00:24:47.500 --> 00:24:49.627
But Bev's interesting, man. She's...


00:24:49.802 --> 00:24:51.269
I'm worried she's bonkers.


00:24:51.437 --> 00:24:54.270
See, my last girlfriend, she was hot,
but absolutely mental.


00:24:54.440 --> 00:24:57.102
I need a girl who's not gonna be
shipped to the loony bin.


00:24:57.276 --> 00:24:59.039
Hang on, I'm gonna hit the facilities.


00:24:59.212 --> 00:25:00.907
Facilities. That's a new one.


00:25:01.347 --> 00:25:04.043
- Hey, man. Sorry we're late.
- Hey, what's good, y'all?


00:25:04.217 --> 00:25:06.947
Nobody talks to my boy
until he comes from the facilities.


00:25:07.120 --> 00:25:08.314
We're here to impress.


00:25:08.488 --> 00:25:10.752
- Clear, right?
- Got it.


00:25:14.594 --> 00:25:17.062
<i>When you're fighting just to keep it sane</i>


00:25:17.230 --> 00:25:19.494
<i>Throw your will
At the eye of the hurricane</i>


00:25:19.665 --> 00:25:21.860
<i>- Sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:22.034 --> 00:25:25.401
<i>- Help me sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:25.571 --> 00:25:28.096
<i>If you wanna find out who you are
Stop running</i>


00:25:28.274 --> 00:25:31.539
<i>In the end you'll figure out
It's all about nothing</i>


00:25:31.711 --> 00:25:37.013
<i>All night, it's gonna be all right
Hey, hey, hey, hey</i>


00:25:37.183 --> 00:25:43.918
<i>All right
Turn your dreams into your life</i>


00:25:45.124 --> 00:25:46.614
That's good.


00:25:53.666 --> 00:25:56.965
I'm clean. No one followed me.
And I got your intel.


00:25:57.804 --> 00:26:00.136
Oh, Katie, baby, your life sucks.


00:26:00.306 --> 00:26:02.206
Trust me, it gets worse.


00:26:03.242 --> 00:26:06.837
Okay, dude, those guys, they
just went Oral Majority on me in there...


00:26:07.013 --> 00:26:09.208
- I was trying to hold them back...
- You're right.


00:26:09.382 --> 00:26:11.316
They have potential and they're great.


00:26:11.484 --> 00:26:16.717
But first, my talent-finding friend,
promise me no more auditions in the bogs.


00:26:16.889 --> 00:26:19.084
- The what?
- The loo.


00:26:19.625 --> 00:26:21.388
- Bathroom. Toilet.
- Got it.


00:26:21.561 --> 00:26:24.155
All right. Okay, come on.
I wanna show you something.


00:26:24.764 --> 00:26:28.063
So now I have to rehearse in secret.


00:26:28.234 --> 00:26:29.701
Why not not rehearse?


00:26:29.869 --> 00:26:31.894
Make Bev sound bad. What do you care?


00:26:32.071 --> 00:26:35.063
No song, no savings account. No life.


00:26:37.243 --> 00:26:39.677
People. Coming. Now.


00:26:43.216 --> 00:26:45.047
Okay.


00:26:45.618 --> 00:26:47.984
Dude, what are we doing?
The suspense is killing me.


00:26:48.321 --> 00:26:50.084
Can you grab the mike?


00:26:50.256 --> 00:26:52.247
Not about to serenade
a brother, are you?


00:26:52.425 --> 00:26:54.256
Dude, with bromance, comes a fine line.


00:26:54.427 --> 00:26:56.725
That I shall not cross.


00:26:57.196 --> 00:26:59.494
So sing something.


00:27:01.167 --> 00:27:02.634
Okay.


00:27:06.772 --> 00:27:09.570
<i>I'm lost in a world
That rattles my brain</i>


00:27:09.742 --> 00:27:12.233
<i>I'm cleaning up my life
From the mess you made</i>


00:27:12.411 --> 00:27:13.810
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:14.280 --> 00:27:16.271
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:18.084 --> 00:27:20.552
<i>My soul's in debt, but my bills are paid</i>


00:27:20.720 --> 00:27:23.245
<i>I'd give anything just to make an escape</i>


00:27:23.422 --> 00:27:25.014
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:25.525 --> 00:27:27.152
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:28.160 --> 00:27:31.095
<i>So you can keep
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:31.264 --> 00:27:33.596
<i>Baby, you're rockin'
But there ain't no way I'm ever letting you in</i>


00:27:33.766 --> 00:27:35.233
<i>He's amazing.</i>


00:27:36.636 --> 00:27:38.297
<i>Not again</i>


00:27:39.238 --> 00:27:42.071
<i>So keep on
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:42.241 --> 00:27:47.440
<i>But, baby, you're better off walking
'Cause I ain't gonna let you in</i>


00:27:47.613 --> 00:27:49.171
<i>Never again</i>


00:27:50.283 --> 00:27:52.877
<i>I went out on a limb again</i>


00:27:53.052 --> 00:27:55.612
<i>I guess I had to lose to win</i>


00:27:55.788 --> 00:28:00.157
<i>I was too confused to know
Which way to turn</i>


00:28:01.561 --> 00:28:04.223
<i>- And she could be a millionaire...
- Crap.</i>


00:28:04.397 --> 00:28:06.661
<i>- Gail needs me to drive her home.
- I don't care</i>


00:28:06.832 --> 00:28:09.494
<i>'Cause, baby, there's nobody home</i>


00:28:09.669 --> 00:28:12.160
<i>Nobody's home at all, yeah</i>


00:28:16.642 --> 00:28:18.769
- What? Did you write that?
- Yeah.


00:28:18.945 --> 00:28:21.573
Reminds me of, um... Uh...


00:28:21.747 --> 00:28:25.080
- Danger Fruit, right? Danger Fruit.
- Ha, ha. Because I wrote their album too.


00:28:25.351 --> 00:28:27.842
Shut up. Took me forever
to find that bootleg online.


00:28:28.020 --> 00:28:30.011
- I love that album. That's crazy.
- Yeah.


00:28:30.189 --> 00:28:32.487
My dad doesn't know.
And he thought the record...


00:28:32.658 --> 00:28:34.353
...was a pile of crap.


00:28:34.627 --> 00:28:36.322
He thinks writing's a waste of time.


00:28:36.762 --> 00:28:40.596
Because he basically wants me
to be like him. Only with better hair.


00:28:41.067 --> 00:28:45.163
But the first thing I thought when
I heard those guys in the urinals was...


00:28:45.338 --> 00:28:46.362
...good acoustics.


00:28:46.772 --> 00:28:50.606
Second thought was these guys,
these guys could be great.


00:28:50.776 --> 00:28:52.368
If you gave them your song.


00:28:53.779 --> 00:28:55.440
Mate, that's a brilliant idea.


00:28:56.182 --> 00:28:58.878
- So put them in the Showcase?
- Put them in the Showcase.


00:28:59.051 --> 00:29:00.382
Yeah.


00:29:02.054 --> 00:29:08.584
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:29:08.894 --> 00:29:10.191
You wrote that song today?


00:29:10.363 --> 00:29:13.821
- You've been home for what, two hours?
- It's like an answer to his song.


00:29:14.100 --> 00:29:15.397
You really like this guy.


00:29:15.568 --> 00:29:17.263
Yeah, I'm an idiot.


00:29:17.436 --> 00:29:19.631
You have to sing that for him.


00:29:19.805 --> 00:29:23.297
What if you sang to him in secret?


00:29:25.111 --> 00:29:27.909
At the dance. Ta-da.


00:29:31.517 --> 00:29:34.350
Okay, I know the card's
like, really cheesy, but...


00:29:36.389 --> 00:29:38.857
Oh, God, I hope you like it.


00:29:39.191 --> 00:29:42.683
Ange, it's beautiful,
but are you crazy?


00:29:42.862 --> 00:29:44.887
No, I know you're crazy.


00:29:45.064 --> 00:29:46.088
Am not.


00:29:47.133 --> 00:29:50.125
- What if he doesn't even like me?
- You'll both be in disguise.


00:29:50.302 --> 00:29:52.998
It's your chance to see
if he was really flirting with you.


00:29:53.172 --> 00:29:55.732
I was naked. Of course he was flirting.


00:29:55.908 --> 00:29:58.604
And why even torture myself?
It's not like I can have him.


00:29:58.778 --> 00:30:00.712
Why not? Tell him how you feel.


00:30:00.880 --> 00:30:04.907
If he feels the same way, you can reveal
your hot self and he won't tell Gail.


00:30:05.284 --> 00:30:08.378
And if he hates the song,
leave the disguise on.


00:30:11.323 --> 00:30:12.847
Okay.


00:30:13.159 --> 00:30:14.751
I'm going to the dance.


00:30:14.927 --> 00:30:16.258
That's my girl.


00:30:16.529 --> 00:30:20.522
<i>Maurice, no, no.
Again, in Français, longer legs.</i>


00:30:20.700 --> 00:30:23.999
I wouldn't go in your closet
for a little while if I were you.


00:30:24.170 --> 00:30:25.933
What? Why?


00:30:26.105 --> 00:30:27.470
Hey. Wake up.


00:30:31.377 --> 00:30:32.935
Katie!


00:30:33.112 --> 00:30:36.548
The cat has pooped in my closet.
I need you to clean it up.


00:30:36.716 --> 00:30:38.206
Go.


00:30:38.384 --> 00:30:40.113
I told you we don't have a cat.


00:30:40.286 --> 00:30:41.617
Angie, heads up.


00:30:43.589 --> 00:30:44.886
Katie!


00:30:50.096 --> 00:30:51.825
What's going on?


00:30:51.997 --> 00:30:53.430
Nothing.


00:30:53.599 --> 00:30:56.727
I am, uh, re-organizing and labeling. I...


00:30:56.902 --> 00:30:59.200
I took up crochet.
Do you want new socks?


00:30:59.371 --> 00:31:03.432
I would make you a sweater, but I hear
that the arms, that they're really hard.


00:31:06.679 --> 00:31:10.843
Oh, you thought you could sneak off
and go to the dance.


00:31:11.016 --> 00:31:13.246
After what you pulled today with Guy.


00:31:13.419 --> 00:31:14.852
Oh, no, no.


00:31:15.020 --> 00:31:17.511
Oh, no, no, no.


00:31:17.690 --> 00:31:19.988
You're on Victor watch tonight...


00:31:20.159 --> 00:31:22.855
...tomorrow night and every night.


00:31:23.028 --> 00:31:24.052
Fun.


00:31:24.230 --> 00:31:27.358
I'll give Victor all the mothering
you don't have time for.


00:31:27.533 --> 00:31:30.934
Oh, I wish you could be my mommy.


00:31:31.804 --> 00:31:33.829
I'm off to my cinnamon colonic.


00:31:37.810 --> 00:31:40.176
Hey. Get down.
You're gonna break yourself.


00:31:40.513 --> 00:31:42.777
Or worse, the furniture.


00:31:43.082 --> 00:31:46.176
Hello?
- Hey.


00:31:46.452 --> 00:31:49.615
- You look like you're having fun.
- Always.


00:31:49.955 --> 00:31:53.015
Well, I couldn't let you not go to the dance
without me.


00:31:53.192 --> 00:31:55.592
Besides, we have six hours
of shirtless Team Jacob.


00:31:55.761 --> 00:31:58.696
So let's just get this party started.


00:31:58.864 --> 00:32:02.891
- So is Victor driving you nuts?
- I swear to you, he's not human.


00:32:03.169 --> 00:32:06.468
I mean, can you really blame him, though?
Just look at this family.


00:32:07.673 --> 00:32:08.970
Victor, what are you doing?


00:32:18.951 --> 00:32:21.215
Oh, no. Great.


00:32:21.387 --> 00:32:23.582
Eh, she actually looks prettier
that way.


00:32:24.190 --> 00:32:27.216
True. Ugh. Whatever.


00:32:28.394 --> 00:32:31.522
Why did I ever think that tonight
could've been something special.


00:32:32.298 --> 00:32:34.562
Think Bev's all over Luke at the dance
right now?


00:32:34.733 --> 00:32:37.031
They're probably making out. See?


00:32:37.203 --> 00:32:40.400
- Victor, give it a rest.
- Just check it out. Come on.


00:32:43.609 --> 00:32:46.237
<i>Luke is gonna produce
whoever wins the Showcase.</i>


00:32:46.412 --> 00:32:49.472
<i>So we need a little insurance.</i>


00:32:49.648 --> 00:32:52.845
<i>- I know what I'm doing, Mother.
Do you?</i>


00:32:53.752 --> 00:32:56.619
I can't take it anymore, okay?


00:32:56.789 --> 00:32:58.848
I'm taking my life into my own hands.


00:32:59.024 --> 00:33:00.116
I'm talking to Luke.


00:33:00.726 --> 00:33:03.217
- Finally.
- Okay, but we have gotta be home...


00:33:03.395 --> 00:33:04.862
...before Gail gets here.


00:33:05.598 --> 00:33:06.929
What about the demon spawn?


00:33:07.099 --> 00:33:08.123
Mm-hm.


00:33:08.300 --> 00:33:09.699
Right.


00:33:10.703 --> 00:33:12.102
Okay, just watch him.


00:33:15.174 --> 00:33:16.436
Hmm.


00:33:21.247 --> 00:33:23.238
Is that all you've got, Angela?


00:33:23.916 --> 00:33:24.940
Ravi?


00:33:26.619 --> 00:33:29.144
My sister could catch that, jerknut.


00:33:29.321 --> 00:33:31.755
Put some nuts in that sack, ref.


00:33:33.893 --> 00:33:36.453
Miss Katie, I am most startled.


00:33:36.629 --> 00:33:37.823
Obviously.


00:33:38.364 --> 00:33:40.855
All right. All right. Don't hate me.


00:33:41.033 --> 00:33:42.591
Okay, don't hate me. I'm sorry.


00:33:42.768 --> 00:33:46.135
But my name ain't Ravi. It's Tony.


00:33:46.672 --> 00:33:49.800
- Tony.
- Tony Gupta from Jersey.


00:33:49.975 --> 00:33:52.637
- From Jersey.
- I am half Indian.


00:33:53.012 --> 00:33:56.413
My friends call me Meatball
because I'm half Italian.


00:33:56.582 --> 00:33:58.447
Truth is I always wanted to be an actor.


00:33:58.817 --> 00:34:00.341
But I never got my shot.


00:34:00.519 --> 00:34:02.749
I'm working at KFC,
and one day, Gail comes in...


00:34:02.922 --> 00:34:05.322
...she's like, "Are you Indian?"
I'm like, "What?"


00:34:05.491 --> 00:34:07.686
She's like, "Are you a guru?"
I'm like:


00:34:07.860 --> 00:34:09.350
"Who is asking?"


00:34:09.628 --> 00:34:12.995
She says, "Someone
who's paying for some spiritual guidance."


00:34:13.165 --> 00:34:15.759
And I'm like, "Whaa! It's a miracle!"


00:34:15.935 --> 00:34:20.304
I finally get a chance to do
a total immersion into a character.


00:34:20.606 --> 00:34:22.870
Real training and I get paid.
Are you kidding me?


00:34:23.042 --> 00:34:25.442
Ravi is my King Lear.


00:34:25.778 --> 00:34:28.406
<i>You wanna hear
the monologue from My Fair Lady?</i>


00:34:28.580 --> 00:34:29.774
- Oy, mate.
- No, thanks.


00:34:30.983 --> 00:34:33.679
I'm sorry I barged in. Whoops.


00:34:36.488 --> 00:34:40.151
Your secret's safe with me, okay?
But I need to ask you a favor.


00:34:40.826 --> 00:34:42.885
- Meatball.
- Ha, Meatball.


00:34:43.062 --> 00:34:45.530
Please watch Victor tonight
so I can go to the dance?


00:34:45.698 --> 00:34:46.756
Are you kidding me? Done.


00:34:48.334 --> 00:34:49.665
Blow it up.


00:34:51.603 --> 00:34:53.161
Thank you.


00:35:02.982 --> 00:35:04.381
Whoa.


00:35:04.550 --> 00:35:07.178
How am I supposed to find Luke
if everybody's got a mask?


00:35:07.353 --> 00:35:10.413
I never said this was
gonna be easy. Let's do some recon.


00:35:11.790 --> 00:35:14.122
I am Assistant Principal
Dorothy Plumberg.


00:35:14.293 --> 00:35:17.524
No drinking. No texting. No kissing.


00:35:20.232 --> 00:35:23.201
Luke? No. Luke Morgan?


00:35:23.369 --> 00:35:26.998
No leaving the premises
and no experiencing joy of any kind.


00:35:27.706 --> 00:35:30.038
Luke? Ugh.


00:35:35.414 --> 00:35:36.847
Where is he?


00:35:37.683 --> 00:35:40.481
That reminds me.
I got a new act for you to listen to.


00:35:40.652 --> 00:35:42.313
- Now?
- No time like it.


00:35:42.488 --> 00:35:44.922
- Dude, not again...
- We're called Big Pain Ticket.


00:35:48.427 --> 00:35:51.988
<i>I wanna kiss your apocalypse</i>


00:35:52.164 --> 00:35:55.497
<i>Wrap you in my Armageddon</i>


00:35:55.667 --> 00:35:57.862
<i>Sing you a twisted serenade</i>


00:35:58.070 --> 00:36:00.800
They're good, but I'm worried
that chain saw's unsafe.


00:36:00.973 --> 00:36:03.407
Dude, the chain saw's,
like, the best part.


00:36:10.215 --> 00:36:11.273
I think I found him.


00:36:11.450 --> 00:36:13.714
Well, he is blond.


00:36:16.822 --> 00:36:19.120
Oh, my God, what is she doing here?


00:36:21.026 --> 00:36:23.324
I hate teenage desperation.


00:36:23.495 --> 00:36:24.894
What are you doing here?


00:36:25.064 --> 00:36:27.897
Oh, honey, the prize pig
doesn't win the blue ribbon...


00:36:28.067 --> 00:36:30.092
...by covering up its third best asset.


00:36:30.269 --> 00:36:33.204
A, what does that even mean
and, B, did you just call me a pig?


00:36:33.372 --> 00:36:35.203
Honey, I saw you making sweet love...


00:36:35.374 --> 00:36:37.842
...to a plate of Swedish meatballs
at the snack table.


00:36:40.279 --> 00:36:42.406
It's now or never, babe.


00:36:43.949 --> 00:36:47.385
- What if she recognizes me?
- I'll distract her. Go.


00:36:47.553 --> 00:36:49.748
- So was I right or was I right?
- You were right.


00:36:49.922 --> 00:36:52.789
You have very cool taste.
Any more auditions in the men's...


00:36:52.958 --> 00:36:54.892
...and you're fired.


00:36:57.930 --> 00:37:01.457
- I know your secret.
- Which secret is that?


00:37:04.069 --> 00:37:05.559
I heard you sing at school.


00:37:05.804 --> 00:37:06.930
You were amazing.


00:37:07.106 --> 00:37:08.164
Do I know you?


00:37:12.511 --> 00:37:15.105
- I wanna show you something.
- What's your name?


00:37:17.449 --> 00:37:19.508
Angela, what are you doing?


00:37:20.152 --> 00:37:22.643
I'd like to make a request.


00:37:27.159 --> 00:37:29.992
I will make your night. I promise.


00:37:30.162 --> 00:37:31.527
Miss Van R.


00:37:32.164 --> 00:37:34.564
Is it true you wanted to be a dancer
when you were younger...


00:37:34.733 --> 00:37:35.927
...but were never good enough?


00:37:37.302 --> 00:37:38.963
Who told you that?


00:37:56.688 --> 00:37:58.121
Well, now, how lovely.


00:37:58.290 --> 00:38:01.487
But I've seen better dancing
in a Filipino prison, sugar.


00:38:01.660 --> 00:38:02.786
Oh!


00:38:02.961 --> 00:38:07.193
Really? Because I think
I just challenged you to a dance battle.


00:38:11.537 --> 00:38:14.631
Would Luke Morgan please pick up
the white courtesy phone?


00:38:14.806 --> 00:38:17.707
Luke Morgan, white courtesy phone.


00:38:22.481 --> 00:38:25.211
Hold on. What is that?
You've never seen a guitar before?


00:38:25.551 --> 00:38:28.247
You hid a guitar in there.
You hiding anything else?


00:38:28.420 --> 00:38:29.682
Follow me.


00:38:34.726 --> 00:38:36.557
Oh, wow.


00:38:39.031 --> 00:38:44.594
Madam, while your exquisite eyes
tell of a radiant, but mischievous beauty...


00:38:45.470 --> 00:38:47.370
...I have grown impatient.


00:38:47.539 --> 00:38:51.236
Off with your veil,
so that I may know the truth.


00:38:52.744 --> 00:38:53.938
Or not.


00:38:56.215 --> 00:38:59.241
I'm hoping this answers
a lot of your questions.


00:39:05.457 --> 00:39:09.018
<i>I can see it from the spark in your eyes</i>


00:39:10.329 --> 00:39:14.561
<i>You believe in all the things
You've denied</i>


00:39:14.733 --> 00:39:18.260
<i>You wanna fly
And leave your worries behind</i>


00:39:18.437 --> 00:39:22.430
<i>Don't you? Don't you?</i>


00:39:24.409 --> 00:39:27.742
<i>Well, now I'm knocking
At your front door</i>


00:39:29.514 --> 00:39:33.211
<i>And I'm looking for the right cure</i>


00:39:33.885 --> 00:39:37.582
<i>I'm still a little bit unsure</i>


00:39:38.056 --> 00:39:40.889
Okay, now take off that veil.


00:39:41.360 --> 00:39:42.452
Uh-uh.


00:42:21.386 --> 00:42:23.980
I think I've blown something.


00:42:24.156 --> 00:42:27.216
Does anyone else smell cinnamon?


00:42:29.828 --> 00:42:31.386
Move it, fatso.


00:42:33.131 --> 00:42:39.730
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:42:40.472 --> 00:42:44.101
Okay, you are blowing my mind.
You have to show me who you are.


00:42:56.655 --> 00:42:58.088
- We have to go.
- What?


00:42:58.256 --> 00:43:00.281
- Come.
- No, Ange.


00:43:00.459 --> 00:43:03.019
In the middle of a really big moment
right now.


00:43:03.195 --> 00:43:05.163
Someone had an accident
and went home.


00:43:07.632 --> 00:43:08.997
I'm so sorry.


00:43:09.701 --> 00:43:10.929
What...? You...?


00:43:11.636 --> 00:43:13.297
Hey. Wait.


00:43:13.472 --> 00:43:14.700
But who are you?


00:43:14.873 --> 00:43:17.467
Over here. Go, go, go.


00:43:25.617 --> 00:43:28.643
- We beat her.
- I love you for this.


00:43:47.105 --> 00:43:49.130
Interesting babysitting attire.


00:43:49.908 --> 00:43:52.843
I should've known
you'd go behind my back again.


00:43:53.278 --> 00:43:56.213
And that Paula Abdul wannabe,
trying to distract me.


00:43:56.548 --> 00:43:58.743
Don't talk about her like that.


00:44:00.752 --> 00:44:03.915
Your friend wants to be a choreographer,
if memory serves.


00:44:04.089 --> 00:44:07.650
She might've made a decent one
if she hadn't gotten herself expelled.


00:44:07.826 --> 00:44:10.090
Guess she can kiss
them Juilliard dreams goodbye.


00:44:10.262 --> 00:44:13.322
Look, I'll do whatever you want.
Okay? Just leave Ange out of this.


00:44:13.632 --> 00:44:16.760
That depends if you pull another stunt
like tonight, sugar.


00:44:17.669 --> 00:44:20.797
- I won't.
- I'll be taking this.


00:44:27.312 --> 00:44:30.543
Only her eyes were piercing out
through this veil, but her voice...


00:44:30.715 --> 00:44:32.774
How hot was the girl
on a scale of one to 10?


00:44:32.951 --> 00:44:34.885
- An 11.
- The hotness scale only goes 10.


00:44:35.053 --> 00:44:36.748
Yeah, this girl has love potential.


00:44:36.922 --> 00:44:39.220
- Ooh, love.
- Shut it.


00:44:40.592 --> 00:44:44.722
We are gonna do this for hours
until we get it right. Even if it takes hours.


00:44:45.697 --> 00:44:49.292
Now, sing like your life depends on it.
Because, sugar, it does.


00:44:50.368 --> 00:44:51.995
We're recording.


00:44:52.304 --> 00:44:54.135
<i>Plug in the mike</i>


00:44:54.306 --> 00:44:55.534
<i>Open the curtain</i>


00:44:56.141 --> 00:44:58.075
<i>Turn on the lights</i>


00:44:58.243 --> 00:44:59.972
<i>I'm through rehearsing</i>


00:45:00.145 --> 00:45:02.477
- Dang, she's good, man.
- Told you, man.


00:45:02.647 --> 00:45:03.875
Check this out, all right?


00:45:04.049 --> 00:45:07.644
Thirty-nine girls in the singing program
which means 85 percent...


00:45:07.819 --> 00:45:09.650
...have music during the sixth period.


00:45:09.821 --> 00:45:11.652
So your girl's in one of those rooms.


00:45:11.856 --> 00:45:13.881
<i>The feeling ignites</i>


00:45:14.059 --> 00:45:15.219
<i>I'm in control</i>


00:45:15.393 --> 00:45:17.361
Oh, cut. Cut.


00:45:17.529 --> 00:45:19.394
That was subpar at best.


00:45:19.564 --> 00:45:22.089
From the top, pretty please.


00:45:22.834 --> 00:45:26.133
<i>Amazing grace</i>


00:45:26.304 --> 00:45:27.862
It's cool, I got this.


00:45:28.039 --> 00:45:30.405
Ladies, all my single ladies.


00:45:30.575 --> 00:45:33.601
My boy Luke here has a special favor
to ask of you, all right?


00:45:33.778 --> 00:45:36.872
He needs vocals
for this big show coming up, so...


00:45:37.048 --> 00:45:38.606
- My name is...
- Luke Morgan.


00:45:39.050 --> 00:45:41.917
You will put me in the Showcase.
Oh, yes, you will.


00:45:42.454 --> 00:45:46.015
- Maybe I could ask you to sing first?
- I am so gonna rock your world.


00:45:46.291 --> 00:45:49.624
<i>I love the way you love me, Luke</i>


00:45:49.794 --> 00:45:52.388
<i>Inside my head every night</i>


00:45:52.564 --> 00:45:55.032
<i>You come and kiss me good night</i>


00:45:55.200 --> 00:45:58.294
<i>Whatever you see is what you get</i>


00:45:58.470 --> 00:46:00.995
Why don't you not suck
and do it again, okay?


00:46:02.741 --> 00:46:07.337
<i>I wanna be with you forever...</i>


00:46:07.512 --> 00:46:10.481
What is going on in here? Disgusting.


00:46:10.649 --> 00:46:13.482
You two boys are not in my class.
Stop. Wait.


00:46:19.524 --> 00:46:22.721
Stop. Wait. Stop.


00:46:41.846 --> 00:46:44.144
<i>I got nothing to lose</i>


00:46:44.315 --> 00:46:45.509
<i>I've been exposed</i>


00:46:45.684 --> 00:46:47.982
<i>I'm paying my dues</i>


00:46:48.153 --> 00:46:49.518
<i>Playing the role</i>


00:46:50.355 --> 00:46:52.482
- Oh, really?
- We are back where we started.


00:46:52.657 --> 00:46:53.783
This is not good.


00:46:55.360 --> 00:46:57.157
That's her. That's her voice.


00:46:57.328 --> 00:46:59.159
Don't think you can get away from me.


00:46:59.330 --> 00:47:01.730
- Step aside. Step aside.
- Please. Wait.


00:47:01.900 --> 00:47:05.336
Okay. But first, why don't you
just both audition for me.


00:47:05.503 --> 00:47:06.527
Listen...


00:47:06.705 --> 00:47:10.141
<i>Luke, you are the one for me, yes you are</i>


00:47:10.308 --> 00:47:11.969
<i>You just don't know it yet</i>


00:47:23.822 --> 00:47:27.815
<i>Make you believe in me</i>


00:47:27.992 --> 00:47:30.984
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:31.162 --> 00:47:34.791
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:34.966 --> 00:47:38.902
<i>That I can be
Anything, anything, anything</i>


00:47:39.070 --> 00:47:42.870
<i>I'll make you believe in me</i>


00:47:43.408 --> 00:47:46.309
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:46.478 --> 00:47:49.538
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:51.349 --> 00:47:53.283
It was you?


00:47:53.952 --> 00:47:57.046
- Oh, sorry to interrupt.
- Oh, no, honey. Interrupt away.


00:47:57.989 --> 00:48:01.823
I didn't think I'd see you. It was killing me.
Because I felt like we connected.


00:48:03.461 --> 00:48:06.487
Excuse me.
Uh, how exactly did you two connect?


00:48:06.664 --> 00:48:09.428
Yeah, how did we? I mean, we did.


00:48:09.601 --> 00:48:11.728
- Through...
- With your lyrics. They just...


00:48:12.370 --> 00:48:15.100
- I can't get them out of my head.
- My lyrics. Yeah.


00:48:15.373 --> 00:48:17.136
Well, how wonderful.


00:48:17.308 --> 00:48:20.675
But, uh, Bev has to prepare
for her Showcase audition.


00:48:20.845 --> 00:48:23.109
Oh, no. She doesn't need to audition.
You're in.


00:48:24.616 --> 00:48:26.413
Do you wanna grab a bite later?


00:48:26.584 --> 00:48:27.676
- Yeah.
Wait.


00:48:28.620 --> 00:48:30.087
You have a date with detention.


00:48:30.255 --> 00:48:31.722
Actually, he has a date with me.


00:48:31.890 --> 00:48:33.619
Dear me, did I not fire you?


00:48:33.792 --> 00:48:36.488
- I have tenure.
- One call and you're wearing a paper hat...


00:48:36.661 --> 00:48:39.789
...that says "Welcome to McDonald's.
How may I take your order?"


00:48:39.964 --> 00:48:41.454
- Five calls.
- Two calls and text.


00:48:41.633 --> 00:48:43.533
Two calls, a text, several long e-mails.


00:48:43.701 --> 00:48:46.499
One text and a Tweet.
- One text and a re-Tweet.


00:48:46.671 --> 00:48:49.037
Oh, for God's sakes,
go lick a chalkboard.


00:48:49.207 --> 00:48:50.674
Fine.


00:48:51.476 --> 00:48:53.000
I hate you.


00:48:56.648 --> 00:49:00.778
Okay. Um, I'd love to write a song with you.
Let's talk about it tonight?


00:49:01.052 --> 00:49:02.986
- I'd love to.
- Okay, you're on.


00:49:09.561 --> 00:49:11.188
I've always wanted to write a song.


00:49:11.362 --> 00:49:14.559
Maybe I'll write about my skin.
They say love tightens your pores.


00:49:14.732 --> 00:49:16.199
What rhymes with pores?


00:49:16.367 --> 00:49:19.165
Chores. Bores. Sores.


00:49:19.337 --> 00:49:21.532
Katie, I've got a new task for you.


00:49:21.706 --> 00:49:23.901
